 """
 Graph isomorphism functions.
+
+Top-level entry points sitting on top of the classic VF2 matchers
+(:class:`GraphMatcher`, :class:`DiGraphMatcher`) and the VF2++
+implementation in :mod:`networkx.algorithms.isomorphism.vf2pp`.
+
+The pre-check helpers (:func:`could_be_isomorphic`,
+:func:`fast_could_be_isomorphic`, :func:`faster_could_be_isomorphic`) are
+designed as cheap *necessary* conditions for isomorphism, usable on every
+graph type NetworkX ships (undirected simple, undirected multi, directed
+simple, directed multi).  Historically the two heavier variants only
+handled undirected simple graphs because they relied on ``nx.triangles``
+and ``nx.number_of_cliques``, both of which raise
+:class:`~networkx.exception.NetworkXNotImplemented` on directed or
+multi-graphs.  They now fall back to a degree-sequence-only check (the
+same as :func:`faster_could_be_isomorphic`) whenever the extra structural
+statistics are not defined for the input graph type, keeping their
+contract intact: ``True`` never guarantees isomorphism, but ``False``
+still guarantees the two graphs are provably non-isomorphic.
+
+All three pre-check helpers optionally accept a ``node_label`` keyword.
+When set, they additionally require that the multiset of label values in
+both graphs coincides, using ``default_label`` for nodes that lack the
+attribute.  This lets :func:`is_isomorphic` reject label-incompatible
+inputs cheaply before dispatching to a full VF2/VF2++ search.
 """
